## Original Content
The chipmaker has told some of its largest customers that the prices of servers containing its AI chips could move more than 15% higher, Bloomberg News reported.

## Summary
Nvidia has reportedly informed some of its largest customers that prices for servers containing its AI chips could increase by more than 15%, according to Bloomberg News. This signals significant upcoming cost increases for companies building out AI infrastructure.

## Key Points
- Nvidia has warned some of its largest customers about impending price increases
- Prices of servers containing Nvidia's AI chips could rise by more than 15%
- The information was reported by Bloomberg News
- The price hikes are tied to demand and costs associated with AI computing hardware


